      "answer": "$\\displaystyle\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\cot\\theta$.",
      "official_mark_scheme_text": "State or imply $\\frac{dx}{d\\theta}=2\\sin2\\theta$ or $\\frac{dy}{d\\theta}=2+2\\cos2\\theta$ — B1.\n\nUse $\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{dy}{d\\theta}\\div\\frac{dx}{d\\theta}$ — M1.\n\nObtain $\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{2+2\\cos2\\theta}{2\\sin2\\theta}$ — A1. Guidance: OE.\n\nUse correct double-angle formulae — M1.\n\nObtain the given answer correctly, $\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\cot\\theta$ — A1. Guidance: AG; must have simplified numerator in terms of $\\cos\\theta$.\n\nAlternative 1: start by using both correct double-angle formulae, e.g. $x=3-(2\\cos^2\\theta-1)$, $y=2\\theta+2\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta$ — M1; state either $dx/d\\theta$ or $dy/d\\theta$ — B1; obtain $\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{2+2(\\cos^2\\theta-\\sin^2\\theta)}{4\\cos\\theta\\sin\\theta}$ — M1 A1; simplify correctly to $\\cot\\theta$ — A1 AG.\n\nAlternative 2: set $t=2\\theta$; state $dx/dt=\\sin t$ or $dy/dt=1+\\cos t$ — B1; use $dy/dx=(dy/dt)\\div(dx/dt)$ — M1; obtain $dy/dx=(1+\\cos t)/\\sin t$ — A1 OE; use correct double-angle formulae — M1; obtain $dy/dx=\\cot\\theta$ — A1.\n\nPrinted total: 5.",
